[{"id":"D5-0001","d":5,"o":"5.2","x":"medium","q":"Attackers are bombarding employees with push-notification MFA prompts at night until someone approves one out of frustration. Which change BEST reduces this risk?","c":["Replace push approval with FIDO2 authenticators","Increase the minimum password length to sixteen","Deliver one-time codes over SMS instead of push","Require users to re-enroll their devices monthly"],"k":""},{"id":"D5-0002","d":5,"o":"5.4","x":"easy","q":"A hospital wants access rights assigned through job functions such as nurse or pharmacist, so that transfers between departments only require changing a user's role membership. Which access control model fits BEST?","c":["Role-based access control","Discretionary access control","Mandatory access control","Rule-based access control"],"k":""},{"id":"D5-0003","d":5,"o":"5.3","x":"medium","q":"Employees access a partner's cloud application by signing in with corporate credentials through SAML federation. During this flow, which party actually authenticates the user?","c":["The partner's application receiving the assertion","The company's identity provider","The SAML assertion exchanged in the flow","The user's web browser handling the redirects"],"k":""},{"id":"D5-0004","d":5,"o":"5.5","x":"easy","q":"An employee who has moved through three departments still holds access granted in every previous role. Which control MOST directly corrects this accumulation?","c":["Multi-factor authentication on all accounts","Password rotation every ninety days","Periodic access reviews that recertify entitlements","Single sign-on across enterprise systems"],"k":""},{"id":"D5-0005","d":5,"o":"5.6","x":"hard","q":"In a Kerberos environment, a user authenticates once in the morning and then opens sessions to several servers all day without re-entering a password. Which component makes this possible?","c":["The ticket-granting ticket issued by the key distribution center","The server's long-term secret key","The password cached on the workstation","A SAML assertion from the domain controller"],"k":""},{"id":"D5-0006","d":5,"o":"5.1","x":"easy","q":"When comparing biometric door-access systems, a vendor advertises the operating point where the false acceptance rate equals the false rejection rate. What is this metric called?","c":["The false acceptance rate","The throughput rate","The failure to enroll rate","The crossover error rate"],"k":""},{"id":"D5-0007","d":5,"o":"5.4","x":"medium","q":"A global firm must let contract reviewers open documents only during business hours, only from managed devices, and only for their assigned region. Which authorization model expresses these conditions MOST naturally?","c":["Role-based access control","Attribute-based access control","Mandatory access control","Per-document access control lists"],"k":""}]
